I’ve found two concrete risks to fix before validation: `run_all.sh` needs per-PF SSH/timeout guards, and the C++ batch bench source has a duplicated key write in the batch frame builder that would break PF-4 after a rebuild. I’m going to patch those first, then tune/validate only bounded PF runs.
  → Add guarded presentation/full performance execution path
  • Fix PF runner correctness and bounded defaults for failing PFs
  • Run safe syntax/presentation checks and bounded host PF probes
  • Update focused pipeline state with Round 3 results
codex
I’m editing `performances/run_all.sh` to make `full` guarded by default while keeping `presentation` as a no-live-benchmark path. The strict mode will still run the real PF scripts, but each PF will have its own timeout, before/during/after SSH probes, elapsed time, and an abort gate if probes repeatedly fail.
